# `Integer.TryParse(s, r)` is normalized in the walker to the out-param desugar
# `((r = Integer.TryParse(s)) != null) OrElse ((r = 0) = Nothing)`, so the
# compiler only ever sees the 1-arg core, which parses to int-or-null.
# VB's narrowing conversions ROUND (banker's) and THROW `OverflowException`
# outside range. All five used to be the same bare `opcode:i32_from_f64`, so
# `CShort` and `CUInt` were literally identical and neither checked anything.
